<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">1 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 1 October, from 331 BCE to 1960.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/darius-iii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/darius-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/331-bce">331 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,356 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alexander defeats Darius III at Gaugamela</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> routed the far larger army of the Persian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-iii">Darius III</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gaugamela">Gaugamela</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>. The victory broke Achaemenid power and opened the road to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persepolis">Persepolis</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persepolis">Persepolis</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-iii">Darius III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1386">1386 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">640 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Wonderful Parliament opens at Westminster</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Called to meet King Richard II's need for money, the Wonderful Parliament met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westminster-abbey">Westminster Abbey</a> but soon turned to reforming his administration. The Lords and Commons united against him and his unpopular chancellor, Michael de la Pole.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-ii-of-england">Richard II of England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westminster-abbey">Westminster Abbey</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1814">1814 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">212 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Congress of Vienna is due to open formally</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s statesmen had gathered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> to redraw the continent after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s fall, and 1 October was fixed for the Congress's formal opening. Its settlement shaped a balance of power that endured for decades.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1880">1880 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">146 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Philip Sousa takes charge of the US Marine Band</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The 25-year-old John Philip Sousa became leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Marine Band. Over the next twelve years he turned it into a celebrated ensemble and began the career that earned him the name 'The March King'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1890">1890 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">136 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress creates Yosemite National Park</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An Act of Congress established Yosemite National Park in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>'s Sierra <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nevada">Nevada</a>, protecting the high country around the Yosemite Valley. John Muir's campaigning had helped make the case for preservation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1949">1949 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">77 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mao Zedong proclaims the People's Republic of China</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">From the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiananmen">Gate of Heavenly Peace</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a> proclaimed the founding of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a>. Communist victory in the civil war placed the world's most populous country under a new regime.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1957">1957 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">69 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">'In God We Trust' first appears on US paper money</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The first US banknotes carrying 'In God We Trust', one-dollar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> certificates, entered circulation. Congress had made the phrase the national motto in 1956, at the height of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> anxieties about 'godless' communism.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1960">1960 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">66 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nigeria gains independence from Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>'s most populous country, became independent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abubakar-tafawa-balewa">Abubakar Tafawa Balewa</a> as prime minister. It was one of seventeen African states to win independence in 1960, the 'Year of Africa'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 1 October <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/severus-alexander"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/severus-alexander.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Severus Alexander</span><span class="tp">208–235</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-england"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-iii-of-england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henry III of England</span><span class="tp">1207–1272</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/el-greco"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/el-greco.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">El Greco</span><span class="tp">1541–1614</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-vi-holy-roman-emperor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-vi-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles VI, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="tp">1685–1740</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/liaquat-ali-khan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/liaquat-ali-khan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Liaquat Ali Khan</span><span class="tp">1895–1951</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jimmy-carter"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jimmy-carter.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jimmy Carter</span><span class="tp">1924–2024</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-weah"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-weah.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George Weah</span><span class="tp">b. 1966</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 1 October <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-tenmu"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-tenmu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emperor Tenmu</span><span class="tp">c. 631–686</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/yaqub-shpata"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Yaqub Shpata</span><span class="tp">d. 1416</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/marsilio-ficino"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/marsilio-ficino.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Marsilio Ficino</span><span class="tp">1433–1499</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-of-austria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John of Austria</span><span class="tp">1547–1578</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mindon-min"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mindon-min.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mindon Min</span><span class="tp">1808–1878</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/abdur-rahman-khan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abdur-rahman-khan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Abdur Rahman Khan</span><span class="tp">c. 1840–1901</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/enrico-de-nicola"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Enrico De Nicola</span><span class="tp">1877–1959</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
